.\" Man page for microagent. The option and environment lists below are checked
.\" against `microagent --help` by `make check-man`, so the two cannot drift.
.TH MICROAGENT 1 "2026-09-30" "microagent 0.8.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
microagent \- tiny OpenAI-compatible coding agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B microagent
.RI [ options ]
.RI "\(dqprompt\(dq"
.br
.B microagent update
.RB [ \-c | \-\-check ]
.br
.B "microagent help"
.RI [ update ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B microagent
runs one non-interactive task of an OpenAI-compatible coding agent: it sends a
task to a provider, calls the tools the model asks for until it stops, and
writes the model's text to stdout. It is a single static binary that links no C
library on Linux; the
.BR search ", " ast " and " git
tools run
.BR rg ", " ast-grep " and " git
from
.BR PATH ,
which a package should depend on.
.PP
The task is the bare argument, or the value of
.BR \-\-print .
Two bare arguments are a usage error rather than a prompt. A bare
.B help
prints the built-in usage text when the prompt is still empty, and
.BI "help " update
prints the subcommand's own text; a word after
.B help
naming no subcommand is a usage error. A bare
.B \-\-
ends the flags, so a task beginning with a dash is passed after it. A bare
.B update
is the subcommand when it is the first argument, and a task of that name
otherwise; it follows a flag or a
.BR \-\- .
.PP
A word that names no flag is answered with the one it is closest to, so
.B \-\-modl
says did you mean
.BR \-\-model ?
A word close to none of them is reported plainly, since naming the least bad of
a dozen is worse than naming none.
.PP
Tools: bash, read, write, edit, multi_edit, search, ast, git, todo, and the
.B skill
loader. The search, ast and git tools call
.BR rg (1),
.BR "ast\-grep" (1)
and
.BR git (1),
so those three have to be on
.BR PATH .
Tools can be removed and MCP servers added in the config file; see
.B FILES
and the full reference in
.IR docs/usage.md .
.SH OPTIONS
Every long option that takes a value also takes it as
.BI \-\-flag= value \fR;
an option that takes none, like
.BR \-\-help ,
names no flag when a value is written on, and is a usage error.
A flag wins over the environment variable for the same option, and over one the
run could not use.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-print " " \fIprompt\fR
Task to run, also accepted as a bare argument.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-model " " \fImodel\fR
Model id sent to the provider. Environment
.BR MICROAGENT_MODEL ,
config key
.BR model ,
default
.BR deepseek/deepseek\-v4\-flash .
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-base\-url " " \fIurl\fR
OpenAI-compatible base url. Environment
.BR MICROAGENT_BASE_URL ,
config key
.BR base_url .
One of the three has to name an endpoint: there is no default provider. https,
or http on loopback, because the api key goes to it in the clear otherwise.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-api\-key " " \fIkey\fR
Api key. Environment
.BR MICROAGENT_API_KEY ,
config key
.BR api_key ;
no key file is read. A key on the command line is in the process table, where
any user of the machine can read it; a variable or a file mode 600 is not.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-turns " n"
Ceiling on tool-loop turns, at least 1. Environment
.BR MICROAGENT_MAX_TURNS ,
default 100.
.TP
.BI \-\-stall\-timeout " s"
Seconds the response socket may stay silent before the read fails. Environment
.BR MICROAGENT_STALL_TIMEOUT ,
default 120.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-tokens " n"
.B max_tokens
sent to the provider, the ceiling on one response's generated tokens, at least
1. Environment
.BR MICROAGENT_MAX_TOKENS ,
default 65536.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
TOML config: system prompt addendum, skills, MCP servers and tools.
Environment
.BR MICROAGENT_CONFIG ,
default
.IR ~/.microagent/config.toml .
.TP
.BI \-\-ca\-bundle " file"
PEM file to trust instead of the system store. Environment
.BR MICROAGENT_CA_BUNDLE ,
else
.BR SSL_CERT_FILE .
Needed in images that ship no ca-certificates.
.TP
.BI \-\-budget " seconds"
Stop starting turns after this long, and say so. At least 1; leaving it out
says "no budget". The last turn it takes may run five minutes past it, and a
turn cut off there is discarded rather than half-applied. Environment
.BR MICROAGENT_BUDGET_SECONDS .
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-spend\-tokens " n"
Stop starting turns once the run has billed this many tokens, prompt and
completion together. At least 1; leaving it out says "no ceiling", the way an
unset
.B \-\-budget
says "no deadline". The turn that reaches the ceiling is the one that finishes,
and the run says on stderr once 80% of it is spent. Environment
.BR MICROAGENT_MAX_SPEND_TOKENS .
.TP
.BI \-\-reasoning\-effort " level"
.B reasoning.effort
sent to the provider:
.BR minimal ,
.BR low ,
.BR medium ,
.B high
or
.B none
to disable. Environment
.BR MICROAGENT_REASONING_EFFORT .
.TP
.BI \-\-temperature " n"
The sampling the provider draws from, 0 to 2. Left out, the field is absent
and the provider samples at its own default, so two runs of one conversation
are two answers; 0 is the one setting under which they are alike. Environment
.BR MICROAGENT_TEMPERATURE .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the built-in usage text and exit. Also reached by a bare
.BR help .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH UPDATE SUBCOMMAND
.B microagent update
downloads
.I microagent\-<tag>\-<target>
and its
.I .sha256
sidecar from the latest GitHub release and replaces the running binary only
when the digest matches. A refusal touches nothing.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-check
Report the latest release as the release page URL on stdout, install nothing.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the update usage text and exit. Also reached by
.BR "help update" .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.PP
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
is a bearer for api.github.com only, past the anonymous rate limit; the public
asset hosts never see it. So does
.BR MICROAGENT_CA_BUNDLE ,
for the same reason it is a run option. Exit 0 checked, installed or current; 1
failed; 2 usage error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MICROAGENT_MODEL
Model id, as
.B \-\-model
says.
.TP
.B MICROAGENT_BASE_URL
Base url, as
.B \-\-base\-url
says.
.TP
.B MICROAGENT_API_KEY
Api key, as
.B \-\-api\-key
says.
.TP
.BR MICROAGENT_MAX_TURNS ", " MICROAGENT_MAX_TOKENS ", " MICROAGENT_STALL_TIMEOUT ", " MICROAGENT_BUDGET_SECONDS ", " MICROAGENT_MAX_SPEND_TOKENS
The ceilings and timeouts above.
.TP
.BR MICROAGENT_REASONING_EFFORT ", " MICROAGENT_TEMPERATURE
As above.
.TP
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
A bearer for api.github.com, for
.B microagent update
only, past the anonymous rate limit. The public asset hosts never see it, and a
run only scrubs it: it is withheld from every tool subprocess a run starts.
.TP
.BR MICROAGENT_CONFIG ", " MICROAGENT_SESSION_DIR ", " MICROAGENT_SKILLS
These three take an empty value as off: no config file, no session log, no
skills.
.TP
.B MDEBUG
Set to 1 to trace a stuck stream on stderr and print the configuration the run
resolved: model, base url, ceilings, the config file read, the skill roots, and
the name of the source the api key came from, never the key.
.TP
.BR NO_COLOR ", " TERM=dumb
The tool gutter draws the tool name in bold on a terminal and in plain text
everywhere else.
.B NO_COLOR
set to anything but an empty string, or
.B TERM=dumb
, leaves the bold out even at a terminal. The value of
.B NO_COLOR
is not read, only the name, and an empty value is not a setting.
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Added to the sandbox writable roots whenever
.B enabled
is true under
.BR [sandbox] ,
on any platform, where it names an absolute directory no root above already
covers. On macOS that is where the system keeps per-user scratch space; a Linux
host exporting it elsewhere gets the same root, and one exporting it at
.I /tmp
gains nothing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.microagent/config.toml
System prompt addendum, repository instructions, skills, MCP servers, tool
set, sandbox and command filter. A first run that finds no config writes the
shipped template here, so the keys are discovered by editing a file that
already documents itself.
.TP
.I ~/.microagent/sessions
Per-response JSONL session log, or
.BR MICROAGENT_SESSION_DIR .
An empty directory writes no log.
.TP
.I ~/.microagent/skills
Skill directories, each holding a
.IR SKILL.md ,
or
.BR MICROAGENT_SKILLS ,
a colon-separated list that wins over the config.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The run finished.
.TP
.B 1
The run failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was wrong.
.TP
.B 3
The run stopped without an answer, so the text on stdout is a prefix of the work
rather than an answer.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by Ctrl+C or a signal, which takes the tool subprocess with it.
.SH OUTPUT
stdout carries the model's text and one JSON line per response,
.BR {\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqusage\(dq,...\(dq} ,
and nothing else. stderr carries the tool gutter, the notes and every error, so
a script reading stdout gets the answer and the token counters.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Fix a failing test and run it:
.PP
.RS
.EX
microagent "fix the failing test in src/net.zig and run it"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Review a diff under a turn ceiling:
.PP
.RS
.EX
microagent --max-turns 20 "review the diff and stop"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run a task whose text is in a file:
.PP
.RS
.EX
microagent --print "$(cat task.txt)"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Pass a task that begins with a dash:
.PP
.RS
.EX
microagent -- "explain why \-Werror is failing in src/net.zig"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Report the latest release without installing it:
.PP
.RS
.EX
microagent update --check
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rg (1),
.BR "ast\-grep" (1),
.BR git (1)
.PP
The full reference, including the config file, the tool set and the sandbox, is
in
.I docs/usage.md
in the source tree. The built-in
.B \-\-help
text is authoritative where this page summarizes.
